# .dockerignore: decides which files Docker may use when building the image.
# Approach: ALLOWLIST. Ignore everything, then allow only what the image needs.
# New files (including secrets like .env) stay out automatically.

# 1) Ignore everything...
*

# 2) ...then allow only what the build needs.

# Backend: application code, database migrations, dependency lists
!backend/app/
!backend/alembic/
!backend/alembic.ini
!backend/pyproject.toml
!backend/uv.lock
!backend/.python-version

# Frontend: source code and build config
# (node_modules is NOT copied; packages are installed fresh inside the image)
!frontend/src/
!frontend/public/
!frontend/index.html
!frontend/package.json
!frontend/package-lock.json
!frontend/tsconfig*.json
!frontend/vite.config.ts

# 3) Even inside allowed folders, never send caches or compiled files.
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache